# Line endings are fixed by the repository, not by each clone's core.autocrlf.
#
# Why: `npm pack` ships the working-tree bytes. On a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true the
# text files check out as CRLF, and the tarball of the same tag gets a different sha1 and
# integrity (ei/v1.40.4: 5f6e1cf6... instead of f6786d2f...) with no functional change - which
# breaks every lockfile that pins the vendored tarball. With eol=lf, any clone on any OS builds
# the same tarball.
#
# text=auto keeps git's binary detection (a file it sees as binary is left untouched).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, explicit.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.tgz  binary
